exists su name brief video script fact one prompt ob text quoted.text.You are writing spoken script lines for a 30-60 second short.

Task:
- Write exactly 2 short spoken sentences.
- Sentence 1: one surprising fact from the transcript.
- Sentence 2: how that fact relates directly to the viewer today.
- Keep this segment between 20 and 44 words.
- Role: establish the first source-grounded lane only.

Rules:
- Dramatic, authoritative tone.
- Source claims must come only from the provided transcript.
- Keep one concrete lane only: one event/reform/mechanism plus one viewer relevance sentence.
- Do not include uplift language, solution language, or final-call language in this segment.
- Prefer wording that stays close to the transcript instead of polished paraphrase.
- Do not turn a broad source description into a stronger causal claim unless that causal wording appears in the transcript.
- Do not introduce new people, places, events, or policies not present in the transcript.
- Do not add summary phrases like "because elites hoarded land" or "survived through reforms" unless the transcript says that directly.
- Do not add exact years, dates, reigns, or named rulers unless that exact detail appears in the transcript.
- If a detail feels uncertain, omit it instead of guessing.
- Plain prose only.
- No labels, no bullets, no markdown, no quotes around the full output.
.text.quoted be text ya

exists su name brief video script fact two prompt ob text quoted.text.You are writing the next spoken segment for the same short.

Task:
- Write exactly 2 short spoken sentences.
- Use a different shocking fact than the one already used.
- Prefer another explicit crisis, fall, or reform example that is plainly stated in the transcript.
- Sentence 1: one surprising fact from the transcript.
- Sentence 2: how that fact relates directly to the viewer today.
- Keep this segment between 20 and 44 words.
- Role: reveal a second lane that is clearly distinct from segment one.

Rules:
- Do not repeat the same person/event/core claim from the prior segment.
- Prefer a clearly different source section than the prior segment.
- Do not reuse the same anchor framing from prior segment (for example the same opening clause or same repeated noun phrase).
- Keep the relation to the viewer different from prior segment (new consequence, risk, or decision frame).
- Fail-safe: if you cannot find a distinct source lane, output exactly: DISTINCT_SOURCE_MISSING.
- Prefer details that can stay close to the transcript's own wording.
- Dramatic, authoritative tone.
- Source claims must come only from the provided transcript.
- Do not use universal or repeated-pattern claims like "every", "always", "never", "consistently", or "after each" unless the transcript says that directly.
- Do not introduce new people, places, events, or policies not present in the transcript.
- Do not synthesize a new source mechanism by combining distant parts of the transcript.
- Do not turn a broad source description into a stronger causal claim unless that causal wording appears in the transcript.
- Do not add summary phrases like "because elites hoarded land" or "survived through reforms" unless the transcript says that directly.
- Do not add exact years, dates, reigns, or named rulers unless that exact detail appears in the transcript.
- If a detail feels uncertain, omit it instead of guessing.
- Plain prose only.
- No labels, no bullets, no markdown, no quotes around the full output.
.text.quoted be text ya

exists su name brief video script uplift prompt ob text quoted.text.Write the ending for the same short.

Task:
- Write 1-2 short spoken sentences.
- Give an uplifting vision grounded in civic courage and reform.
- Keep this segment between 18 and 40 words.
- Role: close and elevate; do not restate source facts from segment one or two.

Rules:
- Hopeful ending.
- No new historical/source facts.
- Do not repeat the same core claim wording from segment one or segment two.
- Prefer consequence-and-invitation language over fact restatement.
- Plain prose only.
- No labels, no bullets, no markdown, no quotes around the full output.
.text.quoted be text ya

exists su name brief video script cta prompt ob text quoted.text.Write one short call to action for this same short.

